 # Captain Notes
 
-## Voyage 3: Row identity and edit-mode controls
+## Voyage 4: Enter commits edit via blur, not directly
 
-Intent: Fix two defects in the todo app — row element identity lost on toggle, and controls visible during editing.
+Intent: Fix edit-commit behaviour so pressing Enter releases focus (calls blur) and the blur handler performs the commit. This ensures commit runs exactly once, fixes trimming, and enables empty-to-delete.
 
-### Defect 1 — Row identity on toggle
-`render()` rebuilds `todoList.innerHTML` from scratch on every state change, destroying and recreating every `<li>`. A reference to a toggled row becomes stale immediately after the click.
-
-Fix: Change `render()` to update existing rows in place — reuse each todo's `<li>`, keyed by the todo, creating/removing only rows that were added/removed. A toggle mutates the row already on the page instead of rebuilding the list.
-
-Discriminating scenario: `features/todo-item.feature` — three new scenarios under Rule "Toggle preserves the list element identity" that capture a reference to a specific `<li>`, toggle, and assert the same element object still carries the updated state.
-
-### Defect 2 — Controls hidden during edit
-When a row is in edit mode (`li.editing`), the `.view` div (checkbox, label, destroy button) remains visible. The app needs a CSS rule at `css/app.css` that hides `.view` inside `li.editing`, so the controls are not visible regardless of where the app is served.
-
-Fix: Add to `css/app.css`: a rule targeting `.view` within `li.editing` to `display: none`.
